# Running this project (read before running any command)

This is a two-part repo. **Commands differ per part and the Python venv is NOT at
the repo root** — a fresh session must follow this exactly instead of guessing.

## Layout & toolchain

- `backend/` — Python **3.14**, FastAPI + background worker, managed by **`uv`**.
  - The virtualenv is at **`backend/.venv`** (gitignored, so it won't show in file
    search). It is **uv-managed** — do **not** `source .venv/bin/activate` or call
    `python`/`pip` directly. On this machine bare `python` does not exist (only `python3`).
  - **Always run Python via `uv run` from inside `backend/`.**
- `frontend/` — Next.js (React 19), managed by **`npm`**. **Always run npm / vitest / next
  from inside `frontend/`.** Running them from the repo root makes Vite/Vitest create a stray
  `node_modules/.vite` cache at the root (there is no root `package.json`).

## Backend commands (run from `backend/`)

```bash
cd backend
uv sync                       # install/refresh deps into backend/.venv
uv run pytest -q              # tests (SQL tests need the Postgres test DB — see below)
uv run ruff check .           # lint
uv run ruff format .          # format
uv run mypy                   # type-check (strict)
uv run alembic upgrade head   # apply DB migrations
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # run the API directly (usually use dev.sh instead)
```

## Frontend commands (run from `frontend/`)

```bash
cd frontend
npm install        # if node_modules is missing
npm run dev        # dev server (http://localhost:3000)
npm test           # vitest
npm run lint       # eslint
npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
npm run build      # next build
```

## Full local stack (preferred for running the app)

From the repo root. This copies env files, starts Postgres + MLflow via Docker,
runs `uv sync` + migrations, and launches API + worker + frontend:

```bash
./scripts/dev.sh              # start everything (Ctrl+C to stop app processes)
./scripts/dev.sh --setup-only # env + Postgres + deps + test DB, no servers (use before tests)
./scripts/dev.sh --stop       # stop orphaned servers on ports 8000/3000
```

## Tests that touch Postgres

SQL tests (`test_*_sql.py` and SQL-backed cases) connect to the **`all_pdfs_chat_test`**
database. Create it first with `./scripts/dev.sh --setup-only`, then:

```bash
cd backend && uv run pytest -q
```

Override the URL if needed via `TEST_DATABASE_URL`.

## Before claiming work is complete

- Backend: `cd backend && uv run ruff check . && uv run mypy && uv run pytest -q`
- Frontend: `cd frontend && npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test`

Reference docs: `README.md`, `backend/backend.md`, `scripts/README.md`.
